WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.416 --> 00:00:14.102
in New York, Mr.

2
00:00:14.142 --> 00:00:15.864
Hobbs was still missing Cedric.

3
00:00:17.665 --> 00:00:21.408
It was the end of the day, and the grocer was sitting alone in his store.

4
00:00:21.428 --> 00:00:25.272
"No one can take Cedric's place," Mr.

5
00:00:25.332 --> 00:00:26.132
Hobbs thought.

6
00:00:26.152 --> 00:00:29.876
"But it would be good to talk to someone besides myself.

7
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.483
Cedric was always mentioning another friend of his—Dick.

8
00:00:35.824 --> 00:00:38.105
Maybe Dick's looking for a new friend too."

9
00:00:41.648 --> 00:00:42.869
The next day Mr.

10
00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.190
Hobbs went for a shoeshine at Dick's stand.

11
00:00:46.531 --> 00:00:49.153
He wasn't quite sure how to start the conversation.

12
00:00:49.173 --> 00:00:53.777
"This is a nice stand," Mr.

13
00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:54.998
Hobbs finally said.

14
00:00:55.018 --> 00:00:58.100
"A friend of mine set me up in business."

15
00:00:59.628 --> 00:01:01.289
Dick applied some polish to Mr.

16
00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:02.230
Hobbs' shoes.

17
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.414
"He was the best little guy you ever met.

18
00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:09.036
He's in England now, learning to be an earl."

19
00:01:09.056 --> 00:01:14.100
"Would that be Lord Fauntleroy?"

20
00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.263
Dick was so surprised that he dropped his cloth.

21
00:01:18.283 --> 00:01:22.007
"Yes! Do you know Cedric too?"

22
00:01:22.027 --> 00:01:26.050
"I've known him since he was born.

23
00:01:27.411 --> 00:01:27.851
I'm Mr.

24
00:01:27.911 --> 00:01:29.564
Hobbs, the grocer."

25
00:01:31.285 --> 00:01:32.165
Dick shook Mr.

26
00:01:32.205 --> 00:01:34.346
Hobbs' hand enthusiastically.

27
00:01:34.366 --> 00:01:37.268
"Cedric told me all about you!"

28
00:01:38.788 --> 00:01:40.049
Mr. Hobbs grinned.

29
00:01:40.069 --> 00:01:43.450
"And I feel like I already know you."

30
00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.611
"I miss Cedric."

31
00:01:48.852 --> 00:01:51.774
Dick picked up his cloth and went back to polishing Mr.

32
00:01:51.814 --> 00:01:52.714
Hobbs' shoes.

33
00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:57.156
"Whenever I was feeling down, he always cheered me up."

34
00:01:58.188 --> 00:01:58.848
"Me too."

35
00:01:59.769 --> 00:02:01.870
Mr. Hobbs nodded in agreement.

36
00:02:03.871 --> 00:02:07.453
Cedric's friends soon realized they had a lot to discuss.

37
00:02:11.116 --> 00:02:14.177
Mr. Hobbs invited Dick to visit him the next evening.

38
00:02:16.038 --> 00:02:18.520
After that the two quickly became friends.

39
00:02:21.842 --> 00:02:25.444
They enjoyed reading Cedric's letters aloud and writing to him.

40
00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.801
Dick often needed help writing letters.

41
00:02:32.502 --> 00:02:33.943
One night he looked over Mr.

42
00:02:33.983 --> 00:02:36.804
Hobbs' shoulder while the grocer edited his letter.

43
00:02:36.824 --> 00:02:40.365
"I didn't have much schooling because I was always working.

44
00:02:41.606 --> 00:02:45.107
I got a job as soon as I was old enough to sell newspapers and run errands."

45
00:02:46.748 --> 00:02:49.089
Mr. Hobbs handed Dick's letter back to him.

46
00:02:49.109 --> 00:02:52.210
"Why did you start working so young?"

47
00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:56.172
"After my parents died, my brother, Ben, took care of me.

48
00:02:57.888 --> 00:03:00.809
He had a job in a store, but we both needed to make money.

49
00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:03.910
Everything was fine until he married Minna."

50
00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.011
Dick rolled his eyes.

51
00:03:07.031 --> 00:03:11.092
"I guess he liked her because she was pretty with long, dark hair.

52
00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:14.053
But she had such a terrible temper!"

53
00:03:15.873 --> 00:03:19.894
After Minna had a baby, she sometimes made Dick take care of him.

54
00:03:19.914 --> 00:03:24.656
"When baby Tom cried, Minna would throw things at me!"

55
00:03:24.956 --> 00:03:25.516
Dick said.

56
00:03:26.732 --> 00:03:28.973
"Like it was my fault that her baby was screaming!"

57
00:03:28.993 --> 00:03:32.454
"She sounds dreadful," Mr.

58
00:03:32.494 --> 00:03:33.214
Hobbs said.

59
00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:37.835
"Once she threw a plate at me and hit the baby instead!

60
00:03:38.756 --> 00:03:40.196
The plate cut Tom's chin."

61
00:03:42.076 --> 00:03:45.517
Dick shook his head as if he still couldn't believe the story.

62
00:03:45.537 --> 00:03:48.778
"The doctor said Tom would always have that scar."

63
00:03:48.798 --> 00:03:51.619
"I hope you don't live with them now."

64
00:03:51.639 --> 00:03:53.940
"Oh, no.

65
00:03:54.396 --> 00:03:56.657
Minna was angry that Ben wasn't making enough money.

66
00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.778
So he went out west to work on a ranch.

67
00:04:01.018 --> 00:04:02.718
A week later Minna and Tom left.

68
00:04:03.639 --> 00:04:05.439
Ben and I never heard from them again."

69
00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:10.540
Soon after the earl's dinner party, Mr.

70
00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.901
Hobbs had an important letter to show Dick.

71
00:04:12.921 --> 00:04:18.102
"Cedric's no longer Lord Fauntleroy!"

72
00:04:18.423 --> 00:04:21.423
the grocer announced as soon as Dick entered the store.

73
00:04:21.443 --> 00:04:23.484
"I don't believe it!"

74
00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:26.445
Dick sat on Cedric's old stool.

75
00:04:27.726 --> 00:04:30.508
Mr. Hobbs began to read Cedric's letter aloud.

76
00:04:31.788 --> 00:04:32.309
Dear Mr.

77
00:04:32.349 --> 00:04:35.791
Hobbs, I have some surprising news for you.

78
00:04:36.871 --> 00:04:38.072
There has been a mistake.

79
00:04:39.633 --> 00:04:43.995
I am not a lord, and I won't be an earl when my grandfather dies.

80
00:04:45.276 --> 00:04:48.818
A woman is saying that she was married to my uncle Bevis.

81
00:04:49.458 --> 00:04:55.401
This means their son is Lord Fauntleroy, because Bevis was the earl's older son.

82
00:04:56.322 --> 00:04:59.823
At first I worried I'd have to give this boy my pony and cart.

83
00:05:01.344 --> 00:05:03.564
But Grandpapa says I may keep them.

84
00:05:03.584 --> 00:05:05.905
(I don't think he likes this woman.)

85
00:05:06.786 --> 00:05:10.907
Grandpapa probably thinks Mama and I are happy I won't be an earl.

86
00:05:12.328 --> 00:05:14.409
But I've grown to like the idea.

87
00:05:15.889 --> 00:05:18.510
You can do so much for people when you're rich.

88
00:05:19.951 --> 00:05:22.112
Sadly, I'm not rich anymore.

89
00:05:23.508 --> 00:05:26.269
I'll have to get a job so I can take care of Mama.

90
00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.872
I'm going to ask the head groom about becoming a groom or a coachman.

91
00:05:33.172 --> 00:05:42.376
Your friend, Cedric Errol (not Lord Fauntleroy) "They're trying to cheat Cedric out of his title because he's

92
00:05:42.396 --> 00:05:43.136
an American!"

93
00:05:44.197 --> 00:05:46.498
Mr. Hobbs pounded his fist on a barrel.

94
00:05:46.518 --> 00:05:48.859
"We have to help him."

95
00:05:48.879 --> 00:05:50.779
"Of course we do!"

96
00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:51.680
Dick said.

97
00:05:52.536 --> 00:05:54.639
"He can be my partner in the shoeshine business."

98
00:05:54.659 --> 00:05:59.285
"And I'll offer him a partnership in the grocery store," Mr.

99
00:05:59.325 --> 00:05:59.985
Hobbs said.

100
00:06:02.088 --> 00:06:07.094
The friends discussed the situation over a supper of biscuits, cheese, and sardines.

101
00:06:09.257 --> 00:06:11.360
Then they wrote Cedric a letter together.
